Package: awscrt
Title: Hardware-Accelerated CRC Checksums from the AWS Common Runtime
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Dyfan", "Jones", , "dyfan.r.jones@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates", role = c("cph"),
           comment = "Author of the bundled aws-checksums and aws-c-common libraries"))
Description: Computes CRC32, CRC32C and CRC64NVME checksums using the
    'aws-checksums' library from the AWS Common Runtime ('CRT'), with runtime
    dispatch to hardware instructions (SSE4.2, PCLMULQDQ, AVX-512, ARMv8 CRC
    and PMULL) and a portable software fallback. Results are returned as
    big-endian raw vectors, matching the bytes the 'S3' flexible-checksum
    headers are built from, and can be chained for incremental hashing.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/awslabs/aws-crt-python
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: GNU make, C compiler
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
